Subject: [PATCH] speech: Google network voices when the build has API keys

A build with Google API keys lists the nineteen remote "Google
<language>" voices in speechSynthesis.getVoices(), as Chrome does. These
voices synthesize through Google's speech API with the build's key, so
the key is what makes them work. The network speech component extension
loads whenever HasAPIKeyConfigured() is true, regardless of branding. A
build without keys lists no network voices, since a listed voice that
cannot speak fails a page's speak() call.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
index e047fdc..0ddb088 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@
 #include "extensions/common/extension_l10n_util.h"
 #include "extensions/common/file_util.h"
 #include "extensions/common/manifest_constants.h"
+#include "google_apis/google_api_keys.h"
 #include "pdf/buildflags.h"
 #include "printing/buildflags/buildflags.h"
 #include "ui/accessibility/accessibility_features.h"
@@ -638,9 +639,23 @@ void ComponentLoader::AddDefaultComponentExtensionsWithBackgroundPages(
   AddAimEligibilityExtension();
   AddGlicExtension();
   AddContextualTasksExtension();
 
-// http://crbug.com/41070702
-#if BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  AddNetworkSpeechSynthesisExtension();
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+// Apostate: upstream compiles this call out of every non-Chrome-branded build
+// (http://crbug.com/41070702), which is why this binary reports zero
+// localService:false voices where every Chrome capture reports nineteen. The
+// extension's own bytes ship regardless — its manifests are included
+// unconditionally by browser_resources.grd — so only the registration was
+// missing.
+//
+// What decides whether those voices can speak is the API key, not the
+// branding: the extension posts to the Google speech endpoint with the key it
+// fetches through chrome.systemPrivate.getApiKey. Gating on the key keeps a
+// keyless build exactly as honest as it is today — no voices listed, none
+// promised — and lets a build configured with keys present the voices it can
+// really serve. Listing a voice that cannot speak is what patch 0043 forbids.
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+  if (google_apis::HasAPIKeyConfigured()) {
+    AddNetworkSpeechSynthesisExtension();
+  }
+#endif  // !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 }
